**Key change in `chequear_forma_evidencia`:** per-transaction precedence. For each tx in order: if evidence tx, check cbid then order; first defective determines motivo.

Current code:
```julia
function chequear_forma_evidencia(A::Admision, b::BloquePost)
    cbid_red = A.pd.P.cbid
    # 1) cbid de ambas cabeceras = red local (RAT-1).
    for tx in b.txs
        tx.tipo == Transicion.TxEvidencia || continue
        ev = tx.evidencia
        ev === nothing && continue
        (ev.id1.cbid == cbid_red && ev.id2.cbid == cbid_red) || return MOTIVO_FORMA_CBID
    end
    # 2) orden canónico estricto por `pre_hash` (EV-04).
    for tx in b.txs
        tx.tipo == Transicion.TxEvidencia || continue
        ev = tx.evidencia
        ev === nothing && continue
        ev.h1.pre_hash < ev.h2.pre_hash || return MOTIVO_FORMA_ORDEN
    end
    return nothing
end
```

New:
```julia
function chequear_forma_evidencia(A::Admision, b::BloquePost)
    cbid_red = A.pd.P.cbid
    for tx in b.txs
        tx.tipo == Transicion.TxEvidencia || continue
        ev = tx.evidencia
        ev === nothing && continue
        # forma completa de esta transacción: cbid → orden canónico
        (ev.id1.cbid == cbid_red && ev.id2.cbid == cbid_red) || return MOTIVO_FORMA_CBID
        ev.h1.pre_hash < ev.h2.pre_hash || return MOTIVO_FORMA_ORDEN
    end
    return nothing
end
```

Wait, but the rule says "para cada una, su forma completa (estructura vigente → cbid → orden canónico)". Since structure is outside this function and applies globally to the block (coinbase etc.), maybe not per-tx. But the order asks per-tx within the evidence check. Fine.

Note: For the directed two-evidence cases, the first evidence's defect determines the reason. So the order of `b.txs` matters. For a block with `[orden_bad, cbid_bad]`, first tx is orden_bad → returns MOTIVO_FORMA_ORDEN. For `[cbid_bad, orden_bad]`, first returns MOTIVO_FORMA_CBID. Good.

