Underflow risk: if r1==0 and we do r2 = r1 - 1 → wraps to typemax. Then r1=0 < r2=typemax, which is ascending, not descending. Better: if r1 == r2, then r1 = r1 + 1 (or set r2 = r1 == 0 ? 1 : r1 - 1). Simpler: after drawing, if r1 > r2 use as is; else swap; if equal, set r2 = r1 - 1 but guard. Let me do:
